rows=json.loads(r'''[{\"item_id\":\"V01\",\"L1\":\"IMPL\",\"confidence\":3,\"evidence_locators\":\"V01/contract/src/main/resources/openapi.json:2257; V01/contract/src/main/resources/openapi.json:1165; V01/impl/src/main/java/io/strimzi/kafka/bridge/http/converter/HttpBinaryMessageConverter.java:46; V01/impl/src/main/java/io/strimzi/kafka/bridge/http/converter/HttpTextMessageConverter.java:48\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ Binary strings represent base64 data. The converter decodes asText without checking node types, unlike the text converter's explicit checks; object/array representations can therefore become empty bytes instead of triggering the documented invalid-record response.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V02\",\"L1\":\"UNDECIDABLE\",\"confidence\":3,\"evidence_locators\":\"V02/contract/rest-api/resources/src/main/resources/openapi/deviceEvent/deviceEvent.yaml:44; V02/impl/service/device/api/src/main/java/org/eclipse/kapua/service/device/management/message/KapuaMethod.java:131\",\"rationale\":\"The supplied action schema is an unrestricted string; the enum belongs to responseCode. SUBMIT survives normalization. The asserted action restriction is absent, so these artifacts establish no attributable deviation.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V03\",\"L1\":\"IMPL\",\"confidence\":3,\"evidence_locators\":\"V03/contract/spec/api.json:422; V03/impl/identity/handler.go:161; V03/impl/identity/handler.go:216\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ Both the contract and parameter annotation name preview_credentials_identifier_similar. The executable query lookup instead uses credentials_identifier_similar, making the handler the inconsistent artifact.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V04\",\"L1\":\"SPEC\",\"confidence\":2,\"evidence_locators\":\"V04/contract/spec/api.json:7; V04/impl/selfservice/strategy/code/strategy_recovery_admin.go:153\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ The handler deliberately parses a duration and rejects nonpositive results; the description imposes no integer-only business rule. The regex appears narrower than the intended duration syntax, excluding useful fractional durations.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V05\",\"L1\":\"SPEC\",\"confidence\":3,\"evidence_locators\":\"V05/contract/rest-api/resources/src/main/resources/openapi/dataMessage/dataMessage-scopeId-datastoreMessageId.yaml:26; V05/impl/rest-api/resources/src/main/java/org/eclipse/kapua/app/api/resources/v1/resources/DataMessagesJson.java:202\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ The endpoint description requests one DataMessage, and the JSON handler explicitly constructs one JsonDatastoreMessage. The collection schema reference contradicts that singular operation and is the likely specification error.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V06\",\"L1\":\"IMPL\",\"confidence\":3,\"evidence_locators\":\"V06/contract/opba-banking-rest-api/src/main/resources/static/tpp_banking_api_pis.yml:90; V06/impl/opba-protocols/xs2a-protocol/src/main/java/de/adorsys/opba/protocol/xs2a/entrypoint/pis/Xs2aGetPaymentStatusEntrypoint.java:53\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ The required product parameter allows multiple products. The bank status call substitutes PAYMENT_PRODUCT_SEPA, so the implementation cannot honor the requested product.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V07\",\"L1\":\"UNDECIDABLE\",\"confidence\":3,\"evidence_locators\":\"V07/contract/rest-api/resources/src/main/resources/openapi/deviceEvent/deviceEvent-scopeId-deviceId.yaml:52; V07/contract/rest-api/resources/src/main/resources/openapi/deviceEvent/deviceEvent.yaml:44; V07/impl/service/device/registry/internal/src/main/java/org/eclipse/kapua/service/device/registry/event/internal/DeviceEventImpl.java:195\",\"rationale\":\"The response references a schema whose action is an unrestricted string. SUBMIT is not prohibited by this contract. The proposition's claimed six-value restriction is unsupported, preventing attribution of a deviation.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V08\",\"L1\":\"IMPL\",\"confidence\":3,\"evidence_locators\":\"V08/contract/src/main/resources/openapi.json:335; V08/impl/src/main/java/io/strimzi/kafka/bridge/http/HttpSinkBridgeEndpoint.java:375; V08/impl/src/main/java/io/strimzi/kafka/bridge/http/HttpSinkBridgeEndpoint.java:398\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ The contract explicitly promises 409 for mutually exclusive subscription modes. doSubscribe checks only conflicting body fields, then subscribes without an existing-assignment guard; its callback also supplies no conflict response on failure.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V09\",\"L1\":\"IMPL\",\"confidence\":3,\"evidence_locators\":\"V09/contract/app/src/main/resources-unfiltered/META-INF/resources/api-specifications/registry/v3/openapi.json:622; V09/impl/app/src/main/java/io/apicurio/registry/rest/v3/impl/AbstractResourceImpl.java:131; V09/impl/app/src/main/java/io/apicurio/registry/rest/v3/impl/IdsResourceImpl.java:88; V09/contract/app/src/main/resources-unfiltered/META-INF/resources/api-specifications/registry/v3/openapi.json:4581\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ REWRITE must produce usable content references. The generated URL targets the documented VersionMetaData endpoint rather than its content endpoint, so the implementation rewrites references to the wrong resource.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V10\",\"L1\":\"IMPL\",\"confidence\":3,\"evidence_locators\":\"V10/contract/opba-banking-rest-api/src/main/resources/static/tpp_banking_api_pis.yml:63; V10/impl/opba-protocols/xs2a-protocol/src/main/java/de/adorsys/opba/protocol/xs2a/entrypoint/pis/Xs2aGetPaymentInfoEntrypoint.java:53\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ The contract exposes a multi-product path parameter, but the information request passes PAYMENT_PRODUCT_SEPA to the bank. The constant overrides the caller's requested product.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V11\",\"L1\":\"IMPL\",\"confidence\":2,\"evidence_locators\":\"V11/contract/opba-banking-rest-api/src/main/resources/static/tpp_banking_api_bank_search.yml:45; V11/impl/core/banking-protocol/src/main/java/de/adorsys/opba/core/protocol/controller/TppBankSearchController.java:42\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ A valid search is documented as returning a result object. The explicit empty-list branch returns a bodyless 404, treating an empty search result as a missing resource without contract support.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V12\",\"L1\":\"SPEC\",\"confidence\":2,\"evidence_locators\":\"V12/contract/spec/api.json:7; V12/impl/selfservice/strategy/link/strategy_recovery.go:160\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ The implementation deliberately accepts positive parsed durations, while the description states only an expiration interval. The single-segment integer regex appears to underdescribe that duration interface; no supplied business rule explains excluding compound or fractional intervals.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V13\",\"L1\":\"IMPL\",\"confidence\":2,\"evidence_locators\":\"V13/contract/swatch-contracts/src/main/resources/META-INF/openapi.yaml:316; V13/contract/swatch-contracts/src/main/resources/META-INF/openapi.yaml:1251; V13/contract/swatch-contracts/src/main/resources/META-INF/openapi.yaml:1904; V13/impl/swatch-contracts/src/main/java/com/redhat/swatch/contract/resource/SubscriptionsExceptionMapper.java:42; V13/impl/swatch-contracts/src/main/java/com/redhat/swatch/contract/resource/DefaultExceptionMapper.java:65\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ ErrorResponse resolves to an Errors object with a required errors array. The exception mappers attach a bare Error entity, omitting that envelope. The explicit response structure favors an implementation wrapping defect.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V14\",\"L1\":\"IMPL\",\"confidence\":3,\"evidence_locators\":\"V14/contract/src/main/resources/api-specs/security-openapi.yaml:280; V14/impl/src/main/java/com/zufar/icedlatte/security/api/AuthSessionService.java:84; V14/impl/src/main/java/com/zufar/icedlatte/common/exception/handler/GlobalExceptionHandler.java:143\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ Missing sessions explicitly require 404. revokeById throws IllegalArgumentException, whereas the supplied 404 mapping handles ResourceNotFoundException; the generic handler maps the thrown exception to 500.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V15\",\"L1\":\"IMPL\",\"confidence\":2,\"evidence_locators\":\"V15/contract/swatch-contracts/src/main/resources/META-INF/openapi.yaml:119; V15/contract/swatch-contracts/src/main/resources/META-INF/openapi.yaml:1251; V15/contract/swatch-contracts/src/main/resources/META-INF/openapi.yaml:1904; V15/impl/swatch-contracts/src/main/java/com/redhat/swatch/contract/resource/ContractsExceptionMapper.java:44\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ The default JSON response requires the Errors envelope. ContractsExceptionMapper serializes Error directly. The required errors array is missing, indicating an implementation response-shape defect.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V16\",\"L1\":\"SPEC\",\"confidence\":2,\"evidence_locators\":\"V16/contract/spec/api.json:718; V16/impl/selfservice/strategy/idfirst/strategy_login.go:188; V16/impl/selfservice/flow/login/handler.go:219\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ Identifier-first login intentionally builds an identifier node with username webauthn autocomplete. The schema enum omits this purposeful feature value; expanding the documented attribute values better preserves the implemented login behavior.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V17\",\"L1\":\"IMPL\",\"confidence\":2,\"evidence_locators\":\"V17/contract/swatch-contracts/src/main/resources/META-INF/openapi.yaml:339; V17/contract/swatch-contracts/src/main/resources/META-INF/openapi.yaml:1251; V17/contract/swatch-contracts/src/main/resources/META-INF/openapi.yaml:1904; V17/impl/swatch-contracts/src/main/java/com/redhat/swatch/contract/resource/DefaultExceptionMapper.java:65\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ The GET operation's default response resolves to a required errors array. The general exception mapper returns one Error as the entity, violating that declared envelope.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V18\",\"L1\":\"SPEC\",\"confidence\":2,\"evidence_locators\":\"V18/contract/rest-api/resources/src/main/resources/openapi/deviceKeystore/deviceKeystore.yaml:18; V18/impl/service/device/management/keystore/api/src/main/java/org/eclipse/kapua/service/device/management/keystore/model/DeviceKeystore.java:33; V18/impl/service/device/management/keystore/internal/src/main/java/org/eclipse/kapua/service/device/management/keystore/model/internal/DeviceKeystoreImpl.java:36; V18/contract/rest-api/resources/src/main/resources/openapi/deviceKeystore/deviceKeystore-scopeId-deviceId.yaml:49\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ The model explicitly identifies the keystore through getId and an id serialization annotation; adjacent operations also use keystoreId. The schema's name property appears to misdescribe that identifier.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V19\",\"L1\":\"UNDECIDABLE\",\"confidence\":1,\"evidence_locators\":\"V19/contract/src/main/resources/openapi.json:14; V19/impl/src/main/java/io/strimzi/kafka/bridge/http/HttpBridge.java:143; V19/impl/src/main/java/io/strimzi/kafka/bridge/http/HttpBridge.java:168; V19/impl/src/main/java/io/strimzi/kafka/bridge/http/HttpBridge.java:286\",\"rationale\":\"CORS installs a root handler and the endpoint reads the body. RouterBuilder internals are absent; these files do not establish whether adding that handler suppresses automatic body processing. The claimed failure cannot be verified.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V20\",\"L1\":\"UNDECIDABLE\",\"confidence\":1,\"evidence_locators\":\"V20/contract/src/main/resources/openapi.json:166; V20/impl/src/main/java/io/strimzi/kafka/bridge/http/HttpBridge.java:168; V20/impl/src/main/java/io/strimzi/kafka/bridge/http/HttpSinkBridgeEndpoint.java:181; V20/impl/src/main/java/io/strimzi/kafka/bridge/http/HttpSinkBridgeEndpoint.java:500\",\"rationale\":\"The contract requires partition input and the handler reads it. CORS adds a root handler, but supplied code does not show RouterBuilder's body-handler defaults. Whether CORS prevents parsing remains unestablished.\"},{\"item_id\":\"V21\",\"L1\":\"SPEC\",\"confidence\":3,\"evidence_locators\":\"V21/contract/spec/swagger.json:1559; V21/impl/session/handler.go:128; V21/impl/session/helper.go:8; V21/impl/session/manager_http.go:94\",\"rationale\":\"⚠️ The malformed annotation says in: authorization; the generated contract places Authorization in